{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:15:15Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 61, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "5-## Summary\n6-\n7:One new read-only status line, `TaskCounts`, placed directly under the\n8-`<h1>Tasks</h1>` title and above `AddTask`. It shows the true open/done\n9-totals (never the filtered subset), pluralizes correctly, and is hidden\n10-during the initial load \u2014 matching acceptance criteria 1\u20133 and 8. No new UI\n11-library, icon, or token system: it reuses the page's existing type scale and\n12-adds one new (computed, AA-passing) muted-grey shade in the same family as\n13-the existing `#6b7780` used for `.loading`/`.empty`.\n14-\n15-## Placement decision\n16-\n17-Two candidates per spec: inside `.list-toolbar` (next to `TaskFilter` /\n18-`ClearCompleted`), or near the `<h1>`. Going with **near the `<h1>`**:\n19-\n20-- `.list-toolbar` today holds exactly two flex children with\n21-  `justify-content: space-between` (`frontend/src/App.css:33-40`). A third\n22-  child changes that layout's balance and its wrap behavior at narrow\n--\n30-## Component\n31-\n32:New file: `frontend/src/components/TaskCounts.jsx`, sibling to\n33-`ClearCompleted.jsx` (same one-prop-object, no-internal-state shape):\n34-\n35-```jsx\n36:export default function TaskCounts({ open, done }) {\n37-  return (\n38:    <p className=\"task-counts\" role=\"status\">\n39-      {open} {open === 1 ? 'task' : 'tasks'} open \u00b7 {done} {done === 1 ? 'task' : 'tasks'} done\n40-    </p>\n41-  )\n42-}\n43-```\n44-\n45-- `role=\"status\"` gives an implicit `aria-live=\"polite\"` + `aria-atomic=\"true\"`\n46-  region: when add/complete/delete/clear-completed change the numbers,\n47-  assistive tech announces the new sentence without moving focus away from\n48-  whatever control the user just used. No other element in this app has a\n49-  live region today, but this is exactly the case ARIA's `status` role\n50-  exists for \u2014 a passive text update caused by an action elsewhere on the\n51-  page.\n52-- Separator is a middle dot (`\u00b7`, U+00B7) \u2014 visually splits the two clauses\n53-  without implying a list or a sentence boundary. Screen readers render it\n--\n73-```jsx\n74-<h1>Tasks</h1>\n75:{!loading && <TaskCounts open={openCount} done={completedCount} />}\n76-<AddTask onAdd={(title, priority) => run(() => api.createTask(title, priority))} />\n77-```\n78-\n79-Import alongside the other component imports:\n80:`import TaskCounts from './components/TaskCounts'`.\n81-\n82-Nothing else in `App.jsx` changes. `visibleTasks`/`sortedTasks`/`filter`\n83:stay untouched \u2014 `TaskCounts` only ever reads `tasks`.\n84-\n85-## CSS \u2014 `frontend/src/App.css`\n86-\n87-Two changes:\n88-\n89-1. Tighten `h1`'s bottom margin so the new line sits snug under the title,\n90-   with the original visual gap now living between the counts line and\n91-   `AddTask`:\n92-\n93-   ```diff\n94-   - h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }\n95-   + h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }\n96-   ```\n97-\n98-2. Add the new rule (place near `.empty, .loading` since it's the same kind\n--\n100-\n101-   ```css\n102:   .task-counts {\n103-     margin: 0 0 1.2rem;\n104-     font-size: 0.95rem;\n105-     color: #5a646c;\n106-   }\n107-   ```\n108-\n109-### Contrast check (new colour pairing)\n110-\n111:`.task-counts` sits directly on the page background (`body { background:\n112-#f6f7f8 }` \u2014 it's not inside a white `.task` card), so that's the pairing to\n113-check, same as `.loading`/`.empty` already on that background today.\n114-\n115-The obvious reuse, the existing muted grey `#6b7780`, **fails**: computed\n116-relative luminance 0.1788 (text) vs. 0.9289 (`#f6f7f8`) \u2192 contrast\n117-**4.28:1**, below the 4.5:1 text minimum. (`.loading`/`.empty` already use\n118-this pairing \u2014 pre-existing, out of scope to fix here per the story's\n119-non-goals, but not a pairing to copy forward into new UI.)\n120-\n121-Darkened to `#5a646c`, same hue/family, adjusted lightness only: computed\n122-luminance 0.1238 vs. 0.9289 \u2192 contrast **5.63:1** \u2014 passes 4.5:1 with\n123-margin. This keeps the \"secondary, muted\" meaning intact rather than\n124-switching to a token (e.g. full-strength `#16191c` body text) that would\n125-read as equally prominent as task titles.\n126-\n--\n132-[Add task...]                    [Add]\n133-```\n134:No counts line at all \u2014 `{!loading && <TaskCounts .../>}` renders nothing.\n135-Matches the existing gate at `App.jsx:60-71` (criterion 8).\n136-\n137-**Populated \u2014 typical (mixed open/done):**\n138-```\n139-Tasks\n140-3 tasks open \u00b7 2 tasks done\n141-[Add task...]                    [Add]\n142-```\n143-\n144-**Populated \u2014 zero tasks (criterion 2):**\n145-```\n146-Tasks\n147-0 tasks open \u00b7 0 tasks done\n148-[Add task...]                    [Add]\n149-```\n--\n174-\n175-**Error** (`error` set, criterion 9): `tasks` retains its last-known value", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_011WqhTyvA9fikXrBX9Dt9vY", "session_id": "6dcc71cd-8fe6-43d5-9dea-cd22fc6362f0"}}
